                <head>308. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>At approximately 10 p.m. on May 30, 1961, three cars stopped the limousine of
                    Generalissimo Trujillo about 9 kilometers outside Ciudad Trujillo on the highway
                    to <hi rendition="#italic">San Cristobal</hi>. Eight assailants from the cars
                    fired 70 rounds of machine gun ammunition into Trujillo, killing him and putting
                    an end to his more than 30 years of rule in the Dominican Republic. (Joint WEEKA
                    No. 23 from Ciudad Trujillo, June 6; Department of State, Central Files,
                    739.00(W)/6-661)</p>
            </div>
